\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Finance Minister Hints At Lowered Growth Rates \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 1998\par 12:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--Malaysia's Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim Sunday signalled that the government may have to revise down its 1998 economic growth forecast in light of the severe depreciation of the ringgit last week. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar gained 17% against the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to around MYR4.60 late Friday. Since the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis began in July, the ringgit has lost 45% of its value. \par \par \uc2  In a significant admission of the economic problems afflicting Malaysia, Anwar revised down economic growth targets for 1998 to 4.0% through to 5.0%, sharply lower than the 8.0%-plus growth rates which the country has enjoyed over the last decade. The International Monetary Fund, however, has forecast economic growth of 2.5% for Malaysia in 1998. \par \par \uc2  Talking to reporters about the growth rates, Anwar said, 'We will have to review the situation in the next few weeks. If the ringgit recovers slightly I don't think we need to review growth estimates for this year.' \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara, has been steadily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ringgit in the past week. \par \par \uc2  '\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is necessary to reflect the economic fundamentals,' Anwar said. 'We haven't been very aggressive, but we haven't allowed it to slide.' \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara first stepped into the market Wednesday when the ringgit was threatening to break through the MYR5.00 per dollar barrier. Anwar declined to say how much the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent. 'We have been very prudent, cautious, and mindful of the fact that foreign reserves have to be substantial.' As of Dec. 31, Malaysia's foreign reserves totaled $21.71 billion. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  11-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1101GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020010914du1b006c7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
