\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit rises against dollar on rupiah's rebound. \b0\par\par\uc2 263 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Jan 9 (Reuters) - The ringgit rose against the dollar in late trading on Friday in line with a sharp rebound in the Indonesian rupiah, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Talk of repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  also limited dollar purchases, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said news of a 700 million ringgit trade surplus for November also helped the ringgit. Malaysia reported a trade deficit of 142 million ringgit in October. \par \par \uc2  "The trade surplus gave players an excuse to cover their positions ahead of the weekend," said a dealer with a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was at 4.5700/6000 to the dollar at 0930 GMT, after falling to 4.7800 in early trade. The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen about 20 percent against the dollar this week. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah rallied to 7,600 to the dollar from a day low of 10,500. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said thin liquidity continued to exaggerate moves, with spreads as wide as 500 points seen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars at around 4.7000 ringgit this morning, dealers said. Bank Negara, which had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last two days to defend the ringgit, was also believed to have checked rates throughout the day, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not been large as market liquidity has dwindled amid worries about Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  They said commercial demand for the dollar would continue to pressure the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  -- Kuala Lumpur Newsroom (603)201 4813; Fax (603)232 6752 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du190990c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
