\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit slips against dollar despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Jan 9 (Reuters) - The ringgit slipped against the dollar in early trading on Friday despite continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars at around 4.7000 ringgit this morning, dealers said. Bank Negara had also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the ringgit in the last two days. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the dollar down but only for a short while. It's back up again," said a dealer with a Malaysian bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0200 GMT, the ringgit was at 4.7600/7900 to the dollar, against 4.7100/7200 late on Thursday in Kuala Lumpur. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the ringgit was pressured by persistent corporate demand for the dollar and weaknesss in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets. \par \par \uc2  They said thin liquidity continued to exaggerate moves, with spreads of up to 500 points seen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that given its weak undertone, the ringgit could soon test its recent low of 4.8800 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar remains well bid and I think it's only a matter of time before dollar/ringgit hit the 5.00 level," a dealer with another local bank said. \par \par \uc2  -- Kuala Lumpur Newsroom (603)201 4813; Fax (603)232 6752 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du19098q2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngbli