\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Negara Malaysia sells dollars - dealers. \b0\par\par\uc2 175 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Jan 9 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trading on Friday to defend the ringgit, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars at around 4.7000 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  "Negara is in again this morning. It hit brokers at 4.7000 and is still in the market," said a dealer with a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the amount of dollars sold by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was again small. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara had also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last two days to check a sliding ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad said on Friday that Malaysia has sufficient reserves to defend the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  "We have a lot of reserves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And we can afford to defend our position without borrowing," he said in a live interview on private television channel TV3. \par \par \uc2  At 0130 GMT, the ringgit was at 4.6500/6800 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603)201 4813; Fax (603)232 6752 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du19098o9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
