\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2 's Mahathir -2: Anwar Says  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Appropriate \b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1998\par 05:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad Thursday dismissed talk the country may impose \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls, and said the ringgit's dramatic decline this week was the result of market forces. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to reporters after attending an official function, the unusually reticent premier said that any trading restrictions on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would further worsen sentiment. \par \par \uc2  At 0344 GMT (10:44 p.m. EST), the dollar had climbed to MYR4.6000, up from MYR4.5130 late Wednesday. Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the ringgit after it plunged to MYR4.8800 Wednesday afternoon, a historic low. \par \par \uc2  'Now there is no proposal for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls,' Mahathir said. 'The introduction of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls will lead to loss of confidence. We cannot now speak about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls.' \par \par \uc2  He put the blame for the ringgit's fall firmly on market forces, instead of blaming \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators and vested foreign interests as he has often done in the past. \par \par \uc2  'We must accept (this depreciation) as the result of market forces. We don't have any control of the market,' Mahathir said. 'Now the market disciplines the goverment, and governments in East Asian countries are being disciplined.' \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim was reported by government news agency Bernama as saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the ringgit was made at 'an acceptable level.' \par \par \uc2  However, he declined to reveal how much Bank Negara had spent to prop up the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 08-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0440GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du1800550\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
