\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit recovers against dollar on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Jan 8 (Reuters) - The ringgit recovered from early lows against the dollar on Thursday following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars from 4.7000 to 4.6000 ringgit this morning, they said. Bank Negara had also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday to defend the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  At 0140 GMT, the ringgit was at 4.5700/6000 to the dollar after falling to a low of 4.7000 earlier. It was around 4.5400 a dollar late on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "We're seeing a bit of dollar selling following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a European bank dealer in Kuala Lumpur. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar buying out of Sydney had earlier weighed on the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  They said thin liquidity continued to exaggerate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements. \par \par \uc2  "Spreads of 200 to 300 points are common these days," a dealer with a Malaysian bank said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said weakness in the Indonesian rupiah could exert renewed pressure on the ringgit, but fears of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would limit dollar purchases. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah fell to a record low of 9,500 to the dollar this morning. \par \par \uc2  -- Kuala Lumpur Newsroom (603)201 4813; Fax (603)232 6752 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du18019cw\par }