\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit/Low -2: Rumored  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Ineffective \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1998\par 07:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit slumped to a new record low against the dollar in early afternoon trading Monday, unaffected by what dealers said was an attempt by the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence the market. \par \par \uc2  Around 0557 GMT (1:57 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at 4.0375 ringgit (MYR) up from MYR3.9730 late Friday. The dollar has so far traded between MYR3.9650 and MYR4.0375. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now lost 37.4% of its value since the Thai baht was floated from its dollar peg in July. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said strong demand for dollars across the region is the main reason for the ringgit's decline Monday. Many investors are buying the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on expectation of increased corporate demand in a few months. \par \par \uc2  Exporters are also keen to hold onto dollars to try and make the most out of them, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It was also widely believed that Bank Negara, the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market in the morning to try and stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A sharp bout of dollar selling drove the dollar down to around MYR3.9800 from MYR4.0200. \par \par \uc2  'It was small volumes, but it happened very suddenly,' a Hong Kong-based dealer said. \par \par \uc2  So far, Bank Negara's move, assuming it was in the market, has had little impact. \par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was influencing trading in another way. Dealers said investors are concerned about a series of mergers in Malaysia's finance sector. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it expects all 35 domestic finance companies to merge by the end of the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  Although officials deny the bank is forcing the merger program through, many market players are concerned that larger, healthier companies may have little choice but to absorb the bad debts incurred by their smaller counterparts. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar could test MYR4.0500 soon. \par \par \uc2  -By James Hookway; 603 292 5254; jhookway@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 05-01-98 \par \par \uc2  0621GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du15002mb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
