\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Slammed Through MYR 4.0 Level - Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By James Hookway \par \uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1998\par 12:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit plunged through the key 4.000 per dollar level Monday on fears that the country's short-term borrowing is higher than previously thought and concerns that a merger program for the financial sector will pile more debt onto stronger lenders. \par \par \uc2  Ambiguous remarks from Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim escalated the sell-off and prompted speculation of a policy split between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the finance ministry. Commenting on the ringgit's losses, Anwar said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  'The policy is to ensure stability, so Bank Negara should keep the option to defend and stabilize the ringgit,' Anwar told reporters. Some market players took this as tacit criticism of Bank Negara. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  watchers found this ironic, given that Bank Negara was widely believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the ringgit's descent when it reached MYR4.0200 per dollar. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it didn't make much headway in the rush for dollars. Bank Negara officials declined to comment on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue. \par \par \uc2  The tide ran against \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  all day. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke the MYR4.0000/dollar psychological barrier early on, dragging the stock market down with it. Heavy dollar-buying sent the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to MYR4.0825 at 1024 GMT (5:24 a.m. EST), and the Composite Index at the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange finished 4.4% or 25.17 points lower at 546.79. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 05-01-98 \par \par \uc2  1104GMT \par \par \uc2  1143 62554 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du15000c0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
