\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Up Early Vs Dollar On Regional Stability \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 1997\par 03:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit is slightly stronger against the dollar in early trading Tuesday as the Japanese yen holds steady against the greenback and the South Korean won continues to strengthen, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Around 0233 GMT (9:33 p.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at 3.8825 ringgit, down from 3.8960 ringgit late Monday. The dollar so far Tuesday has traded between 3.8750 ringgit and 3.8900 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the improved sentiment in northeast Asia is helping to counterbalance continuing corporate demand for dollars in Malaysia. However, the ringgit could easily breach the 3.9000 ringgit/dollar level if either the yen or the won slides back against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'The situation is finely balanced,' a local dealer said. 'The ringgit could go either way at the moment.' \par \par \uc2  With the end of the year approaching, many Malaysian corporates are picking up dollars to pay back short-term foreign denominated loans which come due soon. Dealers said this dollar-buying is expected to continue into Wednesday before a brief respite next week. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players are also looking for indications of how much \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara, has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ringgit. The bank's latest reserves figures are expected to be released next week. \par \par \uc2  -By James Hookway; 603 292 5254; jhookway@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 30-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0255GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokumen