\par\par \b \uc2  Asian Stk Talk/Malaysia -10: Trading Seen Staying Listless \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 1997\par 02:53\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR: Analysts expect trading on the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange to be listless in the coming week with no positive news to boost market sentiment. \par \par \uc2  They said the continuing weakness of the ringgit and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still scaring foreign investors away from the local bourse. \par \par \uc2  Apart from the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  situtation, high domestic interest rates are keeping investors away from the stock market. Analysts said the tight liquidity situation has kept domestic interest rates high, and if not for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rates could have gone even higher. \par \par \uc2  At the late morning fixing Thursday, the widely watched three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate, or Klibor stood at 9.07%, unchanged from Wednesday. This compares with a Nov. 3 rate of 8.68%. \par \par \uc2  High interest rates often encourage investors to shift their money from the stock market to fixed-income instruments, like bonds or fixed deposits. High interest rates also put a damper on most companies' earnings, making their shares less attractive to investors. \par \par \uc2  The slower economic growth forecast for Malaysia in the coming year will also discourage investors from putting their money in stocks, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  They added that news of CIMB Securities Sdn. Bhd., one of Malaysia's top stockbroking firms, being charged with alleged short-selling is also expected to push the market's main index lower in the coming week. \par \par \uc2  Under the Malaysian law, short-selling, the act of selling securities which the seller doesn't own, is illegal. \par \par \uc2  The main KLSE Composite index ended Thursday at 589.18. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0153GMT \par \par \uc2  5044 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtcc09k8w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
