\par\par \b \uc2  Singapore Dollar Lower Late, But Up From Early 52-Mo Low \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 1997\par 09:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE (AP-Dow Jones)-- The Singapore dollar is down against the U.S. dollar in Friday afternoon trading compared to its level late Thursday. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen from its 52-month low seen earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  In early afternoon trading, the U.S. dollar rose to S$1.6250, from S$1.6140 late Thursday, reaching its highest level since July 1993. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar's rise against the Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday paralleled its climb against the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which saw the U.S. dollar hitting an all-time high of 3.84 ringgit, up from 3.73 ringgit late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise was checked around 0700 GMT (2 a.m. EST) by what traders said was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by Bank Negara, \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'There were rumors that Bank Negara was in, so we sold the (U.S.) dollar at 3.85 ringgit. Others joined in and dollar/Sing followed dollar/ringgit down,' said a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a U.S. bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  At 0740 GMT (2:40 a.m. EST) the U.S. dollar is quoted at S$1.6160 and 3.78 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  At these levels, said traders, interest in buying U.S. dollars is beginning to re-emerge. \par \par \uc2  'The (U.S.) dollar is going higher from here,' said one trader. \par \par \uc2  In Singapore's domestic money market, overnight rates on Singapore dollar deposits are offered at 5.125%, up from 5.00% earlier and 4.75% late Thursday. The three-month interbank offered rate is steady at 6.25%. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800; tom.holland@djmarkets.com.sg) \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0808GMT \par \par \uc2  1163 1859 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc509cuq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
