\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2 /Bk Negara/Reserves-2: Indicates No Mkt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 161 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1997\par 09:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday its reserves totaled 61.3 billion ringgit ($1=3.7000 ringgit) as of Nov. 29, down 380 million ringgit from reserve figures released Nov. 15, the government news agency Bernama reported. \par \par \uc2  The figures indicate that Bank Negara has been avoiding direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets over the past two weeks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has continued its steady depreciation since the Thai baht was floated July 2. The ringgit has lost more than 30% of its value since then. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara's total assets, meanwhile, rose to 107.56 billion ringgit from 104.80 billion ringgit in the middle of the month. \par \par \uc2  The amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in circulation rose to 23.21 billion ringgit compared with 22.74 billion ringgit as of Sept. 15, according to Bernama. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-12-97 \par \par \uc2  0836GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtc409a7s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
