\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit firms vs dollar on corporate demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Oct 7 (Reuter) - The ringgit recovered sharply against the dollar on Tuesday on corporate demand and stop-loss selling of the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said dollar sales were triggered by rumours that \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ringgit and fears that \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  might implement a two-tier market, similar to Thailand's system, after Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad's repeated calls for curbs on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  There was confusion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets early on Tuesday when the format on a Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quotation page was mistakenly changed. \par \par \uc2  The changes gave the impression that a two-tier market had been created in the ringgit, Indonesian rupiah and Philippine peso. \par \par \uc2  This mistake was subsequently corrected to reflect global consolidated contributions. \par \par \uc2  "There was a brief panic that a two-tier market may have been implemented. Then came rumours in Singapore of Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which further hit the dollar," said a dealer with a Malaysian bank. "A lot of stop losses were triggered." \par \par \uc2  Some dealers estimated up to $250-300 million may have been sold. \par \par \uc2  At 1000 GMT, the ringgit was at 3.2775/875 to the dollar against its opening around 3.3400. It earlier hit a high of 3.7400 a dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said buying of the ringgit against the Singapore dollar and thin market condition also helped the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  post one of its biggest intra-day gains against the U.S. dollar this year. \par \par \uc2  Malaysian dealers said they had not detected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence. \par \par \uc2  "There was a large corporate order to buy ringgit which was executed by a Bank Negara agent, and I think this prompted talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara does not normally comment on its open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said further corporate selling and liquidation by players caught long could immediately cap the dollar/ringgit at 3.30. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman (603)201 4813; Fax (603)232 6752 \par \par \uc2  -- Email: kuala.lumpur.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dta701l7b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
