\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit/Early -2:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rumors Abound \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 1997\par 05:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was awash with rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy the ringgit, but none felt confident enough to say they felt sure that was the case. \par \par \uc2  A Hong Kong-based dealer said there were growing suspicions that the monetary authorities of Malaysia, Singapore and Indonesia were working together to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  If that were the case, he said, the central banks were probably trying to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from falling much further or, at least, trying to slow the fall. He doubted they were trying to bring about a reversal. \par \par \uc2  A Singapore-based analyst was skeptical about the rumors of a concerted effort on the part of the three countries to check the drop in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , noting that his sources close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied the talk. He said it was probably just a coincidence that the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were strengthening around the same time. \par \par \uc2  A Singapore-based dealer also said that, though the market was rife with speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he had no confirmation. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, the Hong Kong-based dealer said the rumors would keep investors jittery and, therefore, trading would continue to be volatile. He said the dollar would probably trade between 3.1800 ringgit and 3.3200 ringgit during Asian trading. \par \par \uc2  So far the dollar has traded in a wide range, between 3.2450 ringgit and 3.3680 ringgit this morning. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0318GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dta707jtd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
