\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit/Midday -4: Talk Of Negara  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 1997\par 08:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst in Singapore felt confident Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 2.8100 ringgit to try to stop the dollar's advance, but she had no details. Others said they had no proof of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  She didn't believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could keep the dollar from gaining further on the ringgit, however, noting that those pushing the dollar higher 'have more money to spare than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has.' The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent quite a bit of its reserves defending the ringgit in recent months. \par \par \uc2  The analyst thought the dollar could reach 2.8300 ringgit in Asian trading, and then when investors in London and New York start trading, she said 'you will see more pressure.' \par \par \uc2  Overnight, she sees the dollar moving up toward 3.0000 ringgit. Whether it will make it all the way there so soon, however, was unclear, she said, explaining, 'I think Bank Negara Malaysia is very worried and would try to be around.' \par \par \uc2  An emerging markets analyst in Singapore said he was worried about how investors in the stock market would react. The market is closed for the midday break. \par \par \uc2  The analyst felt certain that authorities would cut the statutory reserve requirement of banking institutions, which is now 13.5%. The move would put more money in the market, which should bring down interest rates, and therefore free up still more money for investors to buy stocks with. \par \par \uc2  That would at least boost investor confidence with regard to the stock market. And if foreigners move back into the stock market, they will need ringgit, which could therefore bring support to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0622GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8f061qc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
