\par\par \b \uc2  BANK NEGARA MALAYSIA SELLS DOLLAR/RINGGIT -DEALERS. \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, Aug 8 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell the dollar in late afternoon trade to defend the ringgit following strong bids for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The said Bank Negara sold the dollar/ringgit through an agent bank at 2.6500/10 at 0900 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "The selling was quite aggressive and I think they are still in the market offering dollar/ringgit," said a European bank dealer in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  No confirmation was available from Bank Negara, which does not normally comment on its open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were quite surprised over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the dollar was not rising too fast. \par \par \uc2  "Probably Negara does not want the dollar to go above the recent high of 2.6530," said a dealer with a Malaysian bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0930 GMT, the ringgit was at 2.6498/10 to a dollar, after hitting a high of 2.6520. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit remained under pressure after falling sharply overnight on rumours, later denied, that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Ahmad Mohamed Don had resigned. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara's support of the ringgit followed Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad's remark on Thursday that he was concerned with the sharp fall in the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar bids from offshore players as well as local corporates were evident throughout the day. This was met by some dollar sales by exporters around the 2.6500 level, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said given the current weak fundamentals in Malaysia and bullish dollar sentiment, the ringgit could be heading for 2.70 against the dollar in the near term. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman (603-201 4813) . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8801j2j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
