\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Slightly Higher; Seen Weak Enough \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 1997\par 10:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was up slightly against the U.S. dollar in late trading Wednesday as investors in London picked up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on what one trader there suspected was the feeling that, for now at least, 'ringgit weakness has gone far enough.' \par \par \uc2  In Malaysia, a dealer said she suspected investors feared Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which hasn't been seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for some time, would step in if the dollar rose to 2.6450 ringgit. And that was keeping some from trying to push the dollar higher. \par \par \uc2  But she noted that investors were aware the dollar's general strength against the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should spill over and make it more valuable against the ringgit. 'There's no reason to sell dollars,' the dealer noted. \par \par \uc2  She said there were rumors that bank heads were to meet with Bank Negara Malaysia on Thursday. 'People are worried they might come out with more restrictions,' she said. \par \par \uc2  An economist said there were other rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be meeting with Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim, who is also deputy prime minister, to assess the impact of the curbs imposed Monday in ringgit swap trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers agreed that these rumors were keeping many wary of taking positions. \par \par \uc2  Around 0820 GMT (4:20 a.m. EDT), the dollar was at 2.6325 ringgit, down slightly from 2.6335 ringgit late Tuesday and down still further from 2.6405 ringgit early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded between 2.6305 ringgit and 2.6430 ringgit during the day. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0850GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8605qqa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
