\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia/Swap Curbs/Amplifier -2: Mahathir Hinted At Move \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 August 1997\par 13:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The ringgit has been battered around since mid-May by a speculative attack on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as well as genuine outflows of investors on fears of economic troubles of the same sort rattling Thailand. \par \par \uc2  Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  first fought back by using \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to keep the ringgit from sliding below 2.5250 ringgit/dollar, it was draining its reserves, which fell about 12% in the first two weeks of July. The defense of 2.5250 ringgit was abandoned July 14. \par \par \uc2  U.S. investment bank Merrill Lynch estimated at the time that \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  only has enough reserves for three days of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , assuming that in defending its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't be willing to allow its foreign reserves to fall below a minimum level of three months-worth of import cover. \par \par \uc2  Economists and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts didn't think the fall in the ringgit was damaging enough to require Malaysia to adopt restrictions on ringgit trading and many doubted authorities would move to institute them on fears that it would taint the country's sought-after image as a free financial center. \par \par \uc2  But they also noted that with Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad's tough talk against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators in recent days, he risked damaging his own credibility if he didn't follow through. \par \par \uc2  'Judging by the rhetoric, you would have assumed something would be done,' said Daragh Maher, economist at ING Barings. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, the rhetoric gave many swap market players the chance to adjust positions in the weeks ahead of Monday's move by Bank Negara, traders said. They were thus better prepared than in May, when Thailand's imposition of capital curbs caught many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders by surprise. \par \par \uc2  A senior economist at a foreign brokerage house, who declined to be named, said his sources told him the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fought against imposing controls but Mahathir, who had come home last month from a two-month vacation abroad to find the ringgit about 5% weaker, 'made a lot of noise with them to come up with something.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-08-97 \par \par \uc2  1101GMT \par \par \uc2  1141 62555 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8405rr3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
