\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia PM Attacks On Speculators Reflect Limited Options \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sheila McNulty \par \uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juli 1997\par 14:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--Since Malaysia's Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad returned from a two-month vacation last week to find the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  about 5% weaker, he has fought back the only way economists believe he can - by trying to 'talk up' the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Mahathir has discounted the notion that speculators and investors have been moving out of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of genuine fears about regional economic problems and instead has insisted it has been a politically-motivated response to the decision by the Association of Southeast Asian Nations to admit Burma to the grouping. \par \par \uc2  He has pledged to take action against such 'rogue speculators' and 'anarchists,' singling out prominent U.S. hedge fund operator George Soros in particular. \par \par \uc2  But with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves down 12% in the first two weeks of July, such 'verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' may the only option for Malaysian leaders, economists say. Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , simply can't afford to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  anymore to prop up the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  'These vague threats are a way of introducing uncertainty into the minds of speculators,' says an economist, who declined to be named because of the sensitivity of criticizing government policy in Malaysia. \par \par \uc2  'They are still trying to talk (the ringgit) up.' \par \par \uc2  Over the past few days, Mahathir's cries against speculators has grown increasingly shrill. \par \par \uc2  'We have worked 20 to 40 years to develop our countries to this level and along comes the man with a few billion U.S. dollars and, within a period of two weeks, he has undone almost the work we have done,' Mahathir charged. 'As a result, the poor people in these countries will suffer and these are the people that have to be protected from George Soros, who has so much money and power but (is) totally thoughtless.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1201GMT \par \par \uc2  1146 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7u05lrz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
