\par\par \b \uc2  Troubled regional Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  recover poise. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 1997\par 07:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 22 (Reuter) - Strife torn Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered some of their poise on Tuesday as operators decided it was time to bank some profits on the U.S. dollar's recent sharp rise. \par \par \uc2  Despite calmer and more stable conditions, dealers and economists were still jittery and said the risk to the downside still loomed large for most of the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The market is awaiting the Asian central bankers meeting in Shanghai later this week which could well come up with major league verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities in an attempt to stop the rot. \par \par \uc2  "This wave of contagion hitting the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a relatively long running affair. The danger is that this is a temporary calm we're seeing," said Desmond Supple, head of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at BZW Asia. \par \par \uc2  Supple said the central bankers meeting could yield strong verbal support for the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but added that he did not expect it to result in actual coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There's a broad-based reassessment of risk-reward valuations in the region. Given that genuine funds are leaving as well as speculators, that significantly increases the cost to the real economy of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ringgit received a boost from Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad's displeasure with the recent speculative assault on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  News reports quoted Mahathir, due to return to Malaysia on Tuesday after a two-month absence, as saying there may have been a political agenda behind the recent moves in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "That's a very strong statement from him. So those funds which were very long (dollars) from below the 2.60 level started to take profit," a European bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was quoted at 2.6200 to the dollar at 0445 GMT against 2.6270 at its Kuala Lumpur close on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar firmed above the 1.46 level against its U.S. counterpart as players turned less bearish after the release of better-than-expected trade data on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said wariness of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resistance was also preventing operators from pushing the Singapore dollar down towards 1.47 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  He said local corporates had sold about $100 million from the 1.4635 level, but the U.S. dollar was likely to meet fresh buying interest around 1.4550. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah hovered around the 2,600 to the dollar level after an aggressive speculative attack on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "It's a fight to break the 2,600 resistance level for the rupiah. Singapore players are defending the resistance. We are waiting to see who has more bullets," a U.S. bank dealer in Jakarta said. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah became the latest victim of a speculative attack, plunging about 150 points to a historic 2,665 low against the dollar before staging a marginal recovery on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Indonesian Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad said on Tuesday the attack on the rupiah was not related to fundamentals and the government had no plans to change its monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht lost ground in domestic markets, where players returned from a long weekend fretting about the impending release of data on financial institutions' non-performing loans. The baht was quoted at 30.880/30.980 to the dollar in the local market versus 30.42/30.47 baht late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7m0289e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
