\par\par \b \uc2  ASIAN EXOTICS -  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  stable in late trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 877 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 1997\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 22 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recovered some of their recent losses on Tuesday as operators took profit on the dollar's recent sharp rise. \par \par \uc2  Dealers and economists said there was growing caution ahead of an Asian central bankers meeting at the end of the week but that the risk to the downside still loomed large for most of the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "This wave of contagion hitting the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a relatively long running affair. The danger is that this is a temporary calm we're seeing," said Desmond Supple, head of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at BZW Asia. \par \par \uc2  Supple said the central bankers meeting could yield strong verbal support for the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  but added that he did not expect it to result in actual coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There's a broad-based reassessment of risk-reward valuations in the region. Given that genuine funds are leaving as well as speculators, that significantly increases the cost to the real economy of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ringgit also received a boost from Malaysian Prime Minister Mahathir Mohamad's comments expressing displeasure with the recent speculative assault on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Press reports quoted Mahathir, due to return to Malaysia after a two-month absence on Tuesday, as saying there may have been a political agenda behind the recent moves in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  "That's a very strong statement from him. So those funds which were very long (dollars) below the 2.60 level started to take profit," a European bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  He said the ringgit had already depreciated by over five percent from a recent high of 2.49 and operators were reluctant to push it towards a low of 2.65 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit hit a 38-month low of 2.6450 in London markets on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The moves have been on very thin volume. It's been purely a speculative attack and the market will see that Malaysia's not as bad as perceived," he said. \par \par \uc2  But he added that domestic dollar demand from corporate parties caught out by the dollar's sharp run-up would limit the ringgit's upside and the dollar should find good support at the psychological 2.60 ringgit level for the time being. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was quoted at 2.6170/200 to the dollar at 0415 GMT against 2.6250/300 at its Kuala Lumpur close on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Further south, the Singapore dollar firmed above the 1.46 level against its U.S. counterpart as players turned less bearish after the release of positive trade data on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Singapore's non-oil domestic exports rose a nominal 8.8 percent year-on-year in June against forecasts of a 6.3 percent nominal rise after May's 1.0 percent fall. \par \par \uc2  Comments by government officials predicting a turnaround in global electronics demand in the coming months also supported sentiment, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Electronic exports account for about 70 percent of Singapore's non-oil domestic exports. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said wariness of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resistance was also preventing operators from pushing the Singapore dollar down towards 1.47 to the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  He said local corporates had sold about $100 million from the 1.4630/40 levels but the U.S. dollar was likely to meet fresh buying interest around 1.4550. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah hovered around the 2,600 to the dollar level after falling prey to an aggressive attack on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "It's a fight to break the 2,600 resistance level for the rupiah. Singapore players are defending the resistance. We are waiting to see who has more bullets," a U.S. bank dealer in Jakarta said. He added that local operators were steadily unloading dollars. \par \par \uc2  "If the 2,600 level is broken, the dollar can fall all the way down to as low as 2,570," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He said many operators could be forced to cut losses in the afternoon when London markets open if the rupiah broke the 2,600 resistance level. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah became the latest victim of a speculative attack on Monday, plunging about 150 points to a historic 2,665 low against the dollar before staging a marginal recovery on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Indonesian Finance Minister Mar'ie Muhammad said on Tuesday the attack on the rupiah was not related to fundamentals and that the government had no plans to change its monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht lost ground in domestic markets, where players returned from a long weekend and fretted about the impending release of data on financial institutions' non-performing loans. The baht was quoted at 30.880/30.980 to the dollar in the local market versus 30.42/30.47 baht late Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The baht was fluctuating quite a bit this morning. But the market was thin, so even a small transaction could move the market," a U.S. bank dealer in Bangkok said. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman in Kuala Lumpur (603-206 2323), Mantik Kusjanto in Jakarta (6221 384-6364), Anchalee Koetsawang in Bangkok (662) 652-0642, Lilian Karunungan in Manila (632-841-8937) and Sonali Desai in Singapore (65-8703090) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7m027z2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
