\par\par \b \uc2  KL overnight steady at 8.7 pct, Negara seen lending. \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, July 22 (Reuter) - The overnight interbank rate was steady at 8.7 percent on Tuesday with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Negara seen injecting fresh funds into the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Bank Negara is lending funds at 8.7 percent and this is capping the overnight at that level," said a dealer with a Malaysian bank. \par \par \uc2  Agent banks of Bank Negara were seen lending one-month funds in the morning, pulling interbank rates lower. \par \par \uc2  Earlier, one-month money was at 8.5 percent against 9.0/9.3 percent on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The three-month rate was at 8.0/8.3 percent against 8.0/9.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was room for more downside. \par \par \uc2  "Rates should come off further but the fall is expected to be gradual," said another dealer. \par \par \uc2  He expects the one-month to stablise around 8.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Anwar Ibrahim said last week that Malaysia did not favour a high interest rate regime. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said direction of interbank rates would continue to be determined by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "It's a matter of how quickly Bank Negara wants rates to fall and to what level," one said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara was said to have injected funds over the past week to help ease market tightness. \par \par \uc2  Recent heavy buying of the ringgit by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from speculative attack had caused a liquidity squeeze. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara said on Tuesday its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to 61.9 billion ringgit as at July 15 against 70.71 billion a fortnight earlier, which confirmed market estimates of the size of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Interest rate futures on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monetary Exchange were steady after recent gains. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT, the three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate (KLIBOR) September contract was unchanged at 92.43, or an implied yield of 7.57 percent. \par \par \uc2  The December contract was also unchanged at 92.64, or 7.36 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman (603-201 4813) . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7m027vq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
