\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia/Ringgit Defense/Amplifier -2: Repercussions Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 1997\par 14:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Because the reserves were released in ringgit, they may mask an even steeper drop in foreign reserves in dollar terms because of the plunge in the ringgit's value between June 30 and July 15. One economist said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have spent as much as U.S.$4 billion defending the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  'This is astronomical,' TA's Loh added. \par \par \uc2  'Now you know why they couldn't afford to defend the ringgit any more,' said Sani Hamid, emerging markets analyst at MMS International. 'Ten billion ringgit is a lot to throw down the drain.' \par \par \uc2  Daragh Maher, economist at ING Barings, said the loss highlights the cost of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reveals what little it achieves. \par \par \uc2  And TA's Loh said it will make \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  more difficult in the future. \par \par \uc2  U.S. investment bank Merrill Lynch said in a report Tuesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  only has enough reserves for three days of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , assuming that in defending its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't be willing to allow its foreign reserves to fall below a minimum level of three months-worth of import cover. \par \par \uc2  Economists suspected the revelation could lead to further pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has already been widely criticized for the confusing way in which it announced loan curbs to the property market in April - in an attempt to head off a financial crisis like the one that has rattled Thailand. \par \par \uc2  That announcement of property curbs sparked a sell-off in the stock market that was exacerbated by the subsequent attack on the ringgit. Malaysia's attempts to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and then its sudden desertion of its defenses fueled further selling of stocks, mostly because of confusion about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies. \par \par \uc2  'I think there's going to be some repercussions,' one economist said. He and others said Bank Negara should have realized it was fighting a losing battle, noting that the speculators were taking on the entire region. \par \par \uc2  'Once Thailand caved in and the peso floated, it was hard to see how Malaysia could stem the tide on its own,' TA's Loh said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1234GMT \par \par \uc2  1194 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7m05btv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
