\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia's Bank Negara Allows Ringgit To Slide: Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sheila McNulty \par \uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par 12:15\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--Malaysia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shocked the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Monday when it gave up the vigorous defence of the ringgit it had maintained over the past two months to cap the dollar at 2.5250 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  After the ringgit fell through that level early in Monday's session, without triggering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged on a wave of sell orders. \par \par \uc2  Speculators swiftly drove the dollar up to 2.5500 ringgit - the weakest level the rinngit has traded in about 18 months, according to economists. It was only then that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped back in, capping the dollar with relatively modest sell orders of around $100 million, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers and some economists viewed the move as a tacit acceptance of a de facto ringgit devaluation. At its weakest point, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was down 1.8% from the 2.5047 ringgit/dollar level late Friday. The ringgit recovered some of its losses subsequently to trade around 2.5300 late Monday in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Others suspected Bank Negara was trying to lure in the speculators who have been putting downward pressure on the ringgit since mid-May, amid attacks on other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Thai baht and Philippine peso. \par \par \uc2  They believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is simply biding its time before launching a crushing counter-attack that will force the dollar down towards 2.5000 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  'I think they're trying to squeeze the speculators,' says Neil Saker, head of regional economic research at SocGen-Crosby. 'Bank Negara are quite skilled. They'll certainly win this battle.' \par \par \uc2  He says the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to win the battle quickly, so it can get interest rates back down to more appropriate levels. On Monday, the daily weighted average 3-month interbank rate was at 16.40%, up from 13.40% Friday and at almost double Thursday's level of 8.60%. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1015GMT \par \par \uc2  1136 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7e054h6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
