\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit -2: Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  At 2.5500 \b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par 05:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers generally expressed surprise at Bank Negara's absence from the market in early Monday trading, particularly as they noted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively over the past few months to stop the dollar strengthening above 2.5250 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  'Today's fall in the ringgit is a de facto devaluation,' said a locally based ringgit dealer. \par \par \uc2  Several dealers said the tactics now being adopted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could show that in the wake of recent developments with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara may have accepted that it would now let market forces decide the level of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Other dealers agreed but they also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had helped sow more confusion into the market, as they were widely believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the ringgit fell to 2.5500 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  'It's a cat-and-mouse game again between the Bank and speculators,' the locally based dealer said, and he noted that trading had quieted down dramatically after the rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But dealers said other aspects of Bank Negara's behavior were expected and they noted that while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  openly in the market Monday, they had allowed the Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (Klibor) to continue moving upward. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, at the late morning fixing, the one-month Klibor was at 18.10%, strongly up from 17.10% Friday. The three-month Klibor was at 16.40%, also up from 13.40% Friday, while the six-month Klibor was at 14.20%, also up from 10.70% Friday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0340 GMT (11:40 p.m. EDT), the dollar was at 2.5390 ringgit, up sharply from 2.5047 ringgit Friday, but lower than 2.5485 ringgit at 0145 GMT before Bank Negara's widely suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped the dollar's gains at 2.5500 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected the ringgit to trade in a wide range Monday between around 2.5200 ringgit and 2.5500 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  But several dealers said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could 'hover' around 2.5350 ringgit for most of the day, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier has further confused the market so that many participants have now retreated to the sidelines. \par \par \uc2  So far this morning the dollar has traded between 2.5050 ringgit and 2.5500 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0359GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7e0536t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
