\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit Higher Early On More  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Talk \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juli 1997\par 04:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was up further against the U.S. dollar in early trading Wednesday, as some dealers said Bank Negara may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late overseas trading after the suspected major \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A Hong Kong-based dealer noted that the ringgit had strengthened sharply to around 2.4960 ringgit at close to 2350 GMT (700 p.m. EDT) Tuesday, and he said he thought it was Bank Negara continuing its efforts from late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Some other dealers agreed but they said that this suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in overseas trading was 'very small' compared with the widely believed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Tuesday, which saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sell 'around $1 billion (U.S)' to push the dollar down. \par \par \uc2  Since its low of around 2.4960 ringgit, the dollar has strengthened somewhat, and at 0224 GMT (10:24 p.m. EDT), the dollar was at 2.5036 ringgit, which is still strongly down from 2.5130 ringgit late Tuesday, and 2.5249 ringgit early Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  'The ringgit's strengthening has been led all the way by Bank Negara,' the dealer from Hong Kong said, but noted that since the dollar's low it has gained after market participants sold ringgit to gain from its recent sharp appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers agreed and said that one of the reasons for the large nature of the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Tuesday was fears by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a possible spillover effect on the ringgit after recent rumors of a possible devaluation of the Philippine peso. \par \par \uc2  Over the past few days the dollar has edged ever closer to 2.5250 ringgit, particularly since last week's decision by the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move towards a 'managed float' for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been equally firm in stopping the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciating above this. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0231GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt79051fk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
