\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Bank Negara strikes at ringgit speculators. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Syed Azman \par \uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, July 8 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to flush out ringgit speculators after defending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for nearly two weeks, dealers and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  They said Bank Negara's action sent the dollar down about 200 points against the ringgit within an hour. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Bank Negara began hitting the market just after 0800 GMT in lots of $50 million each time. "They did not face much resistance until dollar/ringgit came down to 2.5100," said a dealer with a Singapore-based U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  At 2.5100, there was some resistance and dollar/ringgit climbed back to 2.5145 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  struck again around 0930 GMT, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It was amazing, it was as if everyone (speculators) had laid down arms after all the efforts (to pull down the ringgit)," said the U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  He said the volumes were not large throughout the afternoon and if Bank Negara stayed in the market in London and New York, where liquidity was low, it could effectively drive out speculative short ringgit positions from the market. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was quoted at 2.5060/70 to a dollar at 1130 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they were not surprised over the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action as dollar/ringgit was trading very close to 2.5250, the level at which Bank Negara had aggressively defended the ringgit, for most of the day. \par \par \uc2  Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , offshore players out of London were seen testing the authorities after acquiring ringgit through swaps to run their long dollar/ringgit positions, they said. \par \par \uc2  "It was a question of who would act or give way first. The battle may have just begun but Bank Negara has demonstrated it's not going to hold back its punches," said research house MMS International in its market commentary. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could have sold more than $2 billion since last week to defend the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Last Wednesday, Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market using its own name for the first time in many years, against its usual practice of using a broker or a bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not be reached for comment. It does not usually comment on its open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The message is: speculators, don't mess around with central banks," said Jimmy Koh, economist with research firm I.D.E.A. in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "This move to wipe out speculators has been on the authorities' agenda," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers and analysts said it was likely the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after squeezing speculators in the spot market, will come with another squeeze in the forward market. \par \par \uc2  "This will force these players who have borrowed ringgit at exorbitant levels to liquidate their positions. This effectively will flush out speculators with dollar/ringgit outright positions from the market," Koh said. \par \par \uc2  The authorities had expressed their concern over local banks' active involvement in the forward market. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a fresh attack on the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had looked imminent as speculators were building up long ringgit positions on the swaps. \par \par \uc2  Such a position would allow speculators to sell ringgit without worrying about being squeezed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7802yo3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
