\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2 's/Reserves-3: July Data Could Show  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1997\par 07:14\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Loh Eng Seng, chief economist at TA Securities Bhd., said the improvement in Bank Negara's reserves indicated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  much, if at all, during the period and, in fact, had recovered from losses incurred during the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's mid-May \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ringgit against an attack by speculators. \par \par \uc2  'We're almost back to where we were at the end of April,' Loh said. At the end of April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gold, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other reserves amounted to 70.93 billion ringgit, but fell to 69.71 billion ringgit at the end of May. \par \par \uc2  Loh said the next set of data might reflect \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara is widely believed to have bought ringgit to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week to again keep at bay speculators who believe the ringgit is overvalued on expectations that Malaysia will soon face some of the financial troubles rattling Thailand. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0514GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7804zq9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
