\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -4: Higher Rates Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1997\par 12:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Another ringgit dealer in Singapore suspected Bank Negara had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with close to US$780 million in hopes of pushing the dollar firmly below the 2.5250 ringgit level. \par \par \uc2  'They were getting pretty annoyed at the perseverance of offshore speculators against their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' he said. \par \par \uc2  He said it was impossible to set a range in which the dollar will trade overnight, noting that while Bank Negara has made it clear it wants the dollar at 2.5130 ringgit or below, 'too many people were looking to buy dollars' to make it clear that will be sustainable. \par \par \uc2  The dealer suspected interest rates might be pushed up to aid Bank Negara in its defense of the ringgit, as they were in mid-May. \par \par \uc2  But Bank Negara didn't openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market Tuesday. At the late morning fixing, the one-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates were at 7.76%, down from 7.80% Monday. The three-month Klibor were at 7.74%, down from 7.78% Monday, while the six-month Klibor were also at 7.74%, down from 7.78% Monday. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark three-month had moved as high as 8.50% after the mid-May attack on the ringgit as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sought to attract investors back into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate, which indicates short-term liquidity conditions, closed at 5.95%, only slightly higher than Monday's 5.80%. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-07-97 \par \par \u