\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -3:Bk Negara Involvement Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1997\par 11:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said local banks were the ones selling dollars for ringgit. But even if local banks were doing the selling, they could be acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they said. Other dealers, however, were sure that Bank Negara was behind the sudden strengthening of the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  '(Bank Negara) is quite aggressively offering 2.5100 (ringgit for the dollar),' said a ringgit dealer in Hong Kong, who declined to be named. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was using up to US$1 billion to push the dollar down to its current levels. \par \par \uc2  A Singapore-based dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  involved the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  'selling several hundred million dollars.' \par \par \uc2  A ringgit dealer in Kuala Lumpur, who declined to be named, said there was strong support for the dollar at 2.5100 ringgit, indicating it wouldn't drop below that level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers have been expecting an attack on the ringgit for the past few weeks, as they believe the speculators that launched a mid-May attack on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  never left the market, despite being beaten down by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Over the past few days, the dollar has edged increasingly closer to 2.5250 ringgit - the level at which dealers have predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the ringgit from weakening any further. \par \par \uc2  Some say worries about Malaysia's fundamentals, spawned by fears that the country might face some of the problems in its property and banking sectors that have rattled Thailand's economy, have aided the speculators by encouraging genuine investors to leave the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly or indirectly as they abandoned the stock market. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara is believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in recent days, but not to the extent some dealers suggested it did Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0938GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7804yrz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
