\par\par \b \uc2  KL interbank rates stay firm on fund outflow. \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, July 7 (Reuter) - Interbank rates stayed firm on Monday, helped by some fund outflows following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There's an outflow today from Bank Negara's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but we're not sure about the size," said a dealer at a Malaysian bank. \par \par \uc2  Banking sources said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an estimated $400 million last week to defend the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they expected interbank rates to stay firm due to a one-billion ringgit Bank Negara bill issue on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Rates started firming on Friday after a surge in swap points, triggered by rumours of a Bank Negara meeting with bank chief executives to discuss the possibility of introducing selective capital controls to defend the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  But banking sources said there was no such meeting. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said certain large commercial banks were seen lending on the one-month with some suspecting that it was on behalf of Bank Negara. \par \par \uc2  One-week money was at 7.30/50 percent against 7.00/50 percent on Friday. \par \par \uc2  One- and three-month money were at 7.50/80 percent against 7.50/60 percent. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate, which ended at 5.80/90 percent on Friday, was expected to trade around 6.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  Interest rate futures on the Malaysia Monetary Exchange were marginally higher. \par \par \uc2  At 0330 GMT, the three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate (KLIBOR) September contract was up two to 92.57, or an implied yield of 7.43 percent. \par \par \uc2  The December contract rose three to 92.73, or 7.27 percent and March 1998 was up two to 92.76, or 7.24 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman (603-206 2323) . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7702wff\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
