\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit/Late -2:No Need For  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  - Dealers \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 1997\par 11:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Although dealers firmly believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was there to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in case it weakened beyond 2.5250 ringgit, they said Bank Negara didn't have to come in Monday. \par \par \uc2  A second ringgit dealer in Hong Kong, who also didn't want to be named, said that was because much of the focus Monday was on the Philippines because of rumors of a potential devaluation in the peso. 'The speculators, maybe, are focusing their attention over there,' he said. \par \par \uc2  He thought that country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be a better target, saying he believed Malaysia's fundamentals were intact, pointing to the trade surplus the country recorded for May, which the Statistics Department reported Monday. \par \par \uc2  'Everything seems to be right on track for Malaysia,' the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  He therefore didn't think anyone would try to weaken the ringgit to the point that the dollar was trading for 2.5250 ringgit or more. 'I don't think people will dare to move it too much from here,' the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  But economists warned against reading too much into the surplus, noting that the long-term trend showed that growth in exports has now fallen behind growth in imports, which they said was a worrying trend and didn't bode well for Malaysia's trade picture. \par \par \uc2  And other dealers said fears about Malaysia's economy remained. 'No doubt we expect further months to show deficits,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the faster growth in imports could be one of the reasons authorities were keeping interest rates high. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 07-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0945GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7704vx1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
