\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Negara  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to protect ringgit. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Syed Azman \par \uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1997\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, July 2 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to protect the ringgit after Thailand announced a managed float of the baht, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It was the first time in many years that Bank Negara used its own name while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. It usually uses a broker or some of Malaysia's biggest banks for its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Negara came out himself to sell the dollar instead of normal exercise of proxy," said a dealer with a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  followed a sharp weakening in the baht after Thailand announced a managed float for the baht from Wednesday, allowing market forces to set the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara bought ringgit at 2.5250 to the dollar, dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weakened to that level on Wednesday and had tested it several times in the past week. Market players said the 2.5280-2.5300 level was viewed as a stronger barrier. \par \par \uc2  However, for the time being, Bank Negara's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept the ringgit from breaking 2.5250, dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 2.5234/44 to the dollar at 0600 GMT from an open of around 2.5230/35. \par \par \uc2  The actual size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not known but dealers believed the amount of dollars sold by Bank Negara was small. \par \par \uc2  No confirmation was available from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which does not usually comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Bank Negara will continue to support the ringgit around 2.5250. I think this time around, the central banks (in the region) will be able to defend their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Dilip Ratha, regional economist with W.I. Carr in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He said the spillover effect of the baht float on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be brief. \par \par \uc2  "It was an unexpected move by the Bank of Thailand. There will be some speculative pressure but it will be short-lived," he said. \par \par \uc2  Economists said after the ringgit came under speculative attack in May, Bank Negara and other regional central banks would not hesitate to show their presence in the market on any sign of an attack on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In May, speculators unloaded the ringgit because of Thailand's financial crisis. Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to stem the ringgit's losses, but dollar sales were done through agent banks. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves fall by 1.4 billion ringgit ($555 million) to 69.7 billion ringgit at end-May compared with a fortnight earlier. \par \par \uc2  Economists were maintaining their forecast of a stronger ringgit in the next six months. \par \par \uc2  They expect the Malaysian unit to trade at 2.47-2.48 to the dollar by the end of the year on the back of strong economic fundamentals and high interest rates in Malaysia. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit hit its strongest level in 17 months of 2.4680 on January 13 this year, after ending 1996 at 2.5305. \par \par \uc2  -- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7202ztq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
