\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Negara sells dollar/ringgit after baht float. \b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, July 2 (Reuter) - Bank Negara Malaysia sold the dollar early on Wednesday after the Bank of Thailand said it would allow a managed float of the baht, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said it was a token resistance set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 2.5250 ringgit to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "Negara came out himself to sell the dollar instead of normal exercise of proxy," said a dealer with a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  This is the first time in years that Bank Negara has used its own name while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. It usually uses a broker or some of Malaysia's biggest banks for its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said Bank Negara was present in the market right from New York on Tuesday evening to Sydney time this morning. It was checking rates through one of \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's big banks. \par \par \uc2  Although the actual size of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not known, dealers believed the amount of dollars sold by Bank Negara was small. \par \par \uc2  No confirmation was available from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which does not usually comment on its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The ringgit slipped to 2.5250 a dollar from its opening around 2.5230/35 after the Thai news and corresponding sell-down in the baht. But Bank Negara's presence helped reverse the ringgit's trend. \par \par \uc2  At 0400 GMT, the ringgit was quoted at 2.5225/35 to a dollar. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya said on Wednesday that effective immediately the country's exchange rate system would be a managed float, whereby the value of the baht would be set by market forces. \par \par \uc2  -- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-206 2323) . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7202zoh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
