\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia/Shrs/Midday-2: Foreign Funds May Flee Market Again \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1997\par 07:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Mohaiyani's Duckett said it's widely expected in the market that if there is a strong spill-over effect from the developments with Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which should also help to buttress the domestic equity market. \par \par \uc2  When Thailand's financial crisis erupted in May, the fall-out was quickly felt in Malaysia as foreign investors pulled out of the region, fearing the occurrence of similar problems elsewhere in Southeast Asia, said analysts. \par \par \uc2  If there is an adverse reaction Thursday among foreign funds from Hong Kong, New York and London, Duckett wondered how much impact it would actually have, as many have already sold down their Malaysian funds, he noted. \par \par \uc2  An senior analyst at Deutsche Morgan Grenfell said foreign funds could remain wary of Malaysia anyway as there's a perception that earnings growth in companies whose stock they pick up could be slowing down. \par \par \uc2  But foreign funds will wait for more developments in the market as a whole before deciding whether or not to commit again a larger share of their portfolios to Malaysian stocks, she added. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, on the scoreboard, local investors have picked up their pace in the market. Advancers are leading decliners 347 to 186, while 165 shares are unchanged and 180 untraded. \par \par \uc2  Volume has doubled over Tuesday's levels, now at a 176.2 million shares, valued at 961.2 million ringgit, compared with midday Tuesday's 87.2 million shares, valued at 831.6 million ringgit ($1=2.5239 ringgit). \par \par \uc2  Among the blue chips, Renong Bhd. is at 3.34 ringgit, up two sen, while Sime Darby Bhd. is at 8.45 ringgit, up 15 sen. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES ASIAN EQUITIES REPORT  02-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0548GMT \par \par \uc2  5038 55110 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020011004dt7200wcq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
