\par\par \b \uc2  Bank Negara Malaysia Seeks  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Stability - Amplifier \b0\par\par\uc2  By Brian Hansford \par \uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 1997\par 13:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  swiftly Wednesday to keep the ringgit from weakening as part of its continuing efforts to ensure stability, given the uncertainty in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Several locally based dealers said they believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold around $100 million shortly after the dollar reached 2.5250 ringgit in early Wednesday trading and to push it back below that level. \par \par \uc2  Although the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came the same day Thailand announced it would adopt a 'managed float' for its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , ringgit dealers said that wasn't the main impetus for Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  They noted that the 2.5250-ringgit level at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was sited is precisely where dealers have been predicting it would come in since mid-May, when the last bout of nervousness about Thailand spilled over and weakened the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although Bank Negara Malaysia bought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pushed up interest rates to fend of speculators at that time, dealers said that, long before this latest announcement by Thailand, the speculators had been preparing to launch a second attack on the ringgit, as proven by the gradual weakening in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday signaled it will continue to defend the ringgit against such an attack. \par \par \uc2  'It would appear that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to make it clear it wants to put a cap on the dollar's gains,' said Chris Tinker, chief treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  'Not surprisingly Bank Negara is seeking to inject some stability into its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amidst a background of regional instability, particularly with the Thai baht,' said Standard Chartered's Tinker. \par \par \uc2  A ringgit dealer based in Singapore said this suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had shown a 'pretty resolute Bank Negara' and he expected the move to continue to keep market participants wary of trying to push the dollar to 2.5250 ringgit, at least for the time being. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1156GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7204xpt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
