\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit rangebound as dollar rise capped at 2.5250. \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, July 1 (Reuter) - The ringgit was rangebound throughout Asian trading as the dollar's rise was again capped at 2.5250, the level at which Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the dollar's failure to break through the 2.5250 level could bring it back down to around 2.5200 though the downside may be limited by the strength in dollar/majors. \par \par \uc2  "Given the dollar/majors firmness, dollar/ringgit should again test 2.5250. But the question is whether the market is ready to push it above the 2.5250 level," said a dealer with a European bank in Kuala Lumpur. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said dollar gains have been capped by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There was continued talk of Bank Negara palcing orders to sell the dollar at 2.5250, they said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to sell an estimated $100 million to support the ringgit at 2.5250 a dollar after a heavy attack on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was also questioning whether Bank Negara will aggressively defend that level especially in the face of a generally firmer dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We believe that, with the knowledge of the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level, the market is not that overly long on dollar/ringgit and is probably well prepared to turn short on any signs of a Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said research house MMS International in its market commentary. \par \par \uc2  "Thus, rather than aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank Negara is seen putting up a token resistance at 2.5250. Bank Negara may prefer a much more effective \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a slightly higher level where it can catch the market long," it said. \par \par \uc2  At 1000 GMT, the ringgit was at 2.5246/50 to a dollar. It closed at 2.5245/55 in Kuala Lumpur on Monday. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman (603-275 6835) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt71036g4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
