\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit seen rising to 2.47 by year-end. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Syed Azman \par \uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1997\par 09:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, July 1 (Reuter) - The Malaysian ringgit remained under pressure from selling by offshore players as well as concern over the Thai baht, but its weakness was seen as temporary, economists said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Strong economic fundamentals and high interest rates in Malaysia would pull the ringgit out of the slump, they said, expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hit 2.47-2.48 per dollar by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was quoted at 2.5240/50 a dollar at midday on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the ringgit has still not overcome the spillover effect of the baht crisis. The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under severe attack by speculators in May which prompted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the region's central banks. \par \par \uc2  "It's still pretty uncertain in Thailand. Baht sentiment is still pretty negative," said Sim Moh Siong, economist with Citibank in Singapore. "But the comparison between Thailand and Malaysia may not be justified." \par \par \uc2  Acting Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim said last month that the impact of the baht crisis would be temporary. The ringgit should not fall much "because the context of the Thai baht is different and the economic fundamentals are different," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Until we see stability in the baht, there will be a cloud over the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Desmond Supple, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at BZW in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Friday to support the ringgit at 2.5250. \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said there was talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had placed more orders to sell the dollar at that level. \par \par \uc2  Economists said that by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had reaffirmed its preference for a strong ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was unlikely to weaken above 2.5300, they said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 17-month high of 2.4680 on January 13, this year after ending 1996 at 2.5305. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the ringgit was currently undervalued and did not reflect the country's economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "The economy is still among the strongest in the region and barring any fallout from the baht, the ringgit should trade below the 2.50 level," Supple said. \par \par \uc2  "We are looking at 2.47 by year-end," he said. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian Institute of Economic Research, a government-backed think-tank, on Monday maintained its projection of Malaysia's real gross domestic product (GDP) growth at 8.2 percent in 1997 and 8.5 percent in 1998. GDP growth in 1996 was 8.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  Economists said the interest rate differential would also favour the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Though local interbank rates have fallen from their highs in May, they were still much higher than those in neighbouring Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The benchmark three-month Kuala Lumpur interbank offered rate stood at 7.50 percent on Tuesday, about four percentage points higher than in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  Some money market dealers said rates were being kept high by Bank Negara to ward off speculators because it would be expensive to maintain short ringgit positions. \par \par \uc2  "Interest rates in Malaysia have limited scope to come down because of the strong economy. And this should favour the ringgit," said Sim of Citibank. He expects the ringgit to trade at 2.48 a dollar by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt71036ag\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
