\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit Higher Early;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Continue \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juli 1997\par 04:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was higher against the U.S. dollar in early trading Tuesday after the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to pierce 2.5250 ringgit in overnight trading on continued market fears of Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  around this level. \par \par \uc2  A Singapore-based dealer said the market knows 'how serious Bank Negara is about speculators' so market participants were buying or selling in 'bits-and-pieces' with no clear direction so far Tuesday, although, like other dealers, he didn't think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday. \par \par \uc2  A locally based dealer said that while the dollar had 'hovered around' 2.5248 ringgit for some time close to 2200 GMT (6 p.m. EDT) in overseas Monday trading, the fact that it had failed to break 2.5250 ringgit meant that the dollar could weaken Tuesday to 2.5210 ringgit as participants sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cash in to benefit from its recent gains. \par \par \uc2  Another Singapore-based dealer said that a further reason the dollar could drop to around 2.5210 ringgit Tuesday is market participant wariness ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve meeting later in the day, in which it's widely expected that U.S. interest rates won't be changed. \par \par \uc2  Around 0156 GMT (9:56 p.m. EDT), the dollar was at 2.5232 ringgit, down from 2.5245 ringgit late Monday and 2.5238 ringgit early Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded between 2.5228 ringgit and 2.5243 ringgit so far this morning. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0204GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7104wcp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
