\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit down as mkt braces for Negara  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 319 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Previous\tab Forecast\tab Resistance    Support\par     2.5198/5250   2.5220/70     2.5200\tab   2.5280\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  * Market sells down ringgit, but braces for Bank Negara's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 2.5250 \par \par \uc2  * Ringgit's gains late on Friday due to Bank Negara's presence, say dealers \par \par \uc2  * Selling of ringgit prompted by slight weakening of Malaysian interbank money rates \par \par \uc2  * Chartists say dollar/ringgit poised to break 2.5250/60, this year's high \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, June 30 (Reuter) - The ringgit continued to be sold down on Monday morning by big offshore players, but more cautiously on fear that there may be a fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 2.5250 a dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to sell around $100 million to support the ringgit at 2.5250 a dollar after a heavy attack on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  No confirmation was available from Bank Negara, which does not comment on its open market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The market looks poised to test 2.5250 again," said a dealer with a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday brought dollar/ringgit down to 2.5220 by Monday morning, but not for long. It retreated soon after on technical and speculative selling pressure. \par \par \uc2  "The selling is probably because of the fall in interbank rates in Malaysia. The one month has dipped quite a bit and Bank Negara is seen focusing on interbank rates," a dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "This is sending mixed signals to people," he added. \par \par \uc2  An analyst with a Singapore-based research house said the volumes on Friday suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not very big. \par \par \uc2  "It could have been a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bluff. People will test the level againt to see if Bank Negara is really in," he said. \par \par \uc2  At 0235 GMT, the ringgit was at 2.5233/43 to a dollar. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy (603-201 4813) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6u03549\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
