\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit Unchanged On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 1997\par 05:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was unchanged against the U.S. dollar in early trading Friday, on continued market concerns over possible Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 2.5250 ringgit, but also corporate interest in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has kept it from weakening. \par \par \uc2  A ringgit dealer based in Singapore said the dollar's rise was still being 'capped by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears' of market participants who are wary that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciating above 2.5250 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  A locally-based dealer agreed with this view but also said that the dollar hadn't weakened much over these concerns because there was still come corporate 'end-of-June demand' for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from companies who repatriate profits from Malaysia at the mid-year point back to the U.S. \par \par \uc2  At around 0247 GMT (10:47 p.m. EDT), the dollar was at 2.5228 ringgit, unchanged from late Thursday and barely changed from 2.5226 ringgit early Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Most dealers said continued market participant anxiety over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 2.5250 ringgit would likely continue to keep Friday trading in a relatively narrow range so that the dollar will trade between 2.5200 ringgit and 2.5245 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  At 2.5250 ringgit per dollar, the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have lost nearly all the gains it made during the powerful rally that started in early 1997. The ringgit hasn't traded that low since Jan. 2, 1997, when it was at 2.5267 ringgit/dollar and about to embark on a climb that took it as high as 2.4680 ringgit on Jan. 13, 1997. \par \par \uc2  The level is also important because Bank Negara was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ringgit when it approached 2.5250 ringgit/dollar in mid-May, when the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened during the speculative attack on the Thai baht. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded between 2.5208 ringgit and 2.5230 ringgit so far this morning. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0302GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6r04r4d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
