\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia/3Q Stock Outlook -3: Big Impact From Thailand \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1997\par 07:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  'In general, our revised profit estimates for the banking and property sectors are down by about 10% for 1998,' says an analyst with a local brokerage firm who spoke on condition of anonymity. \par \par \uc2  With these new restrictions, Malaysian authorities moved to head off a banking and property crisis similar to the one currently rattling Thailand. \par \par \uc2  But while Bank Negara Malaysia is aiming to forestall the worst excesses of its northern neighbor, it was powerless to prevent the knock-on effect from Thailand's mid-May \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis from affecting the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't publicly comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but dealers widely believe Bank Negara stepped in to stop the dollar strengthening above 2.5250 ringgit on May 14, in a 'spillover effect' from speculators attacking the Thai baht. In a related move, economists also say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates to further support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  such that the benchmark three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates, known as Klibor, rose from pre-increase levels of 7.36% on May 14 to 8.50% on May 20, the highest level for several years. \par \par \uc2  The Klibor has now started to come down, but many analysts worry that Thailand's continued economic problems will make Bank Negara continue to fear possible spillover \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  attacks, and so it will keep interest rate levels high, a scenario analysts say isn't good for the country's stock market. \par \par \uc2  'We may have to sit through higher rates for longer than originally expected,' says Crosby's Lai. \par \par \uc2  Rising interest rates are generally seen as negative for the stock market because they encourage investors to withdraw their investments and place them in risk-free investments such as savings accounts, which give them better yields. \par \par \uc2  Economists also say high interest rates tend to discourage borrowing, which in turn leads to a slowdown in economic growth. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0525GMT \par \par \uc2  1134 62550 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6q04l26\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
