\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit Steady Early On Mkt Fears Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1997\par 04:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was barely changed against the U.S. dollar in early trading Thursday. Although Bank Negara didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight, market fears of such an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped keep the dollar from piercing 2.5250 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Several dealers noted that the highest the dollar reached was 2.5243 ringgit at around 1400 GMT (10:00 a.m. EDT) Wednesday, but they said anxiety over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon brought the dollar back closer to its levels in late Wednesday local trading. \par \par \uc2  Around 0200 GMT (10:00 p.m. EDT), the dollar was at 2.5226 ringgit, little changed from 2.5223 ringgit late Wednesday, but up from 2.5203 ringgit early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A locally-based dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the dollar's appreciation has again been gradual, boosted by mid-year corporate demand for dollars as the end of June approaches. \par \par \uc2  The dealer also said there had been 'selling ahead' of any possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had so far served to keep the dollar below 2.5250 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say that 2.5250 ringgit is an important level because Bank Negara was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the ringgit when the dollar approached 2.5250 ringgit in mid-May, when the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened during the speculative attack on the Thai baht. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say market participants are still wary that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around this level of 2.5250 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  But many dealers also add that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators could still move against the ringgit 'just to test Bank Negara.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0218GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6q04k65\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
