\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2  Ringgit Lower After Rumored  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Overnight \b0\par\par\uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1997\par 04:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was down against the U.S. dollar in early trading Tuesday, but it was higher than its levels in late overseas trading Monday as several dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight to keep the dollar from strengthening above 2.5200 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  A locally-based dealer said the ringgit had weakened in overseas trading late Monday, 'possibly on the back of some profit-taking' by market participants to take advantage of the ringgit's recent gains. \par \par \uc2  The dealer said this may then have encouraged some participants to 'test the 2.5200 ringgit level,' noting that the dollar had very briefly appreciated to 2.5220 ringgit in overseas trading at 2134 GMT (0534 pm EDT) Monday, but it had then fallen back to 2.5158 ringgit at 2342 GMT. \par \par \uc2  A Singapore-based dealer said with 'this rumored mild \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' Bank Negara was again sending a message to any potential speculators that it continued to monitor the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels very closely. \par \par \uc2  At around 0239 GMT (1039 pm EDT), the dollar was at 2.5177 ringgit, up from 2.5155 ringgit late Monday but little changed from 2.5173 ringgit early Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that trading would continue to be quiet Tuesday with many market participants remaining uncertain of the market's direction, such that the dollar would trade between 2.5160 ringgit and 2.5195 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore-based dealer said the dollar could touch 2.5200 ringgit but he didn't think it would remain there because most market participants would be even more wary of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  actions given the rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded between 2.5165 ringgit and 2.5188 ringgit so far this morning. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0251GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6o04mq6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
