\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia \highlight\uc2 /Bank Negara -2: Shows Less  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -Economist \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 1997\par 10:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Daragh Maher, an economist at ING Baring Securities (Singapore) Pte. Ltd., said the increase in Bank Negara's gold, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other reserves seemed to show that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  very much in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market recently. \par \par \uc2  'While the increase in foreign reserves is only marginal, it does indicate that Bank Negara has not had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so aggressively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the ringgit,' said Maher. \par \par \uc2  As reported earlier, Maher said the previous half-month's decline in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gold, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other reserves had partly been caused by Bank Negara's efforts to support the ringgit in the latter part of May. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara Malaysia announced June 10, its gold, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and other reserves added up 69.71 billion ringgit as of May 31, down from 71.13 billion ringgit on May 15, 1997. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara used its reserves to buy ringgit, and also pushed up interest rates, to protect the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it had weakened in a spillover effect from speculators who were also attacking the Thai baht in mid-May. \par \par \uc2  The attack weakened the ringgit beyond the point where, on May 14, the U.S. dollar was fetching 2.5245 ringgit which dealers said forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts paid off and the ringgit regained some of its strength against the dollar, so that it was trading at for 2.4865 ringgit two days later on May 16. \par \par \uc2  Since then, and despite continued economic problems in Thailand, many dealers say that while Bank Negara has continued to monitor the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely, it hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in any major way, if at all, as the fear of speculators seems to be abating and the ringgit hasn't weakened dramatically. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0832GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6k04jkf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
