\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit -2: Reverberations From Baht Crisis :Dealer \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1997\par 11:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said although the dollar had continued to perform well against the majors, Wednesday trading had been subdued with market participants unsure of the market's direction. \par \par \uc2  A locally-based dealer noted that the dollar had consecutively risen then fallen between around 2.5175 ringgit and 2.5185 ringgit for much of Wednesday afternoon trading, with participants alternately buying then quickly selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gain on its appreciation. \par \par \uc2  The locally-based dealer said he thought market participants were still wary about the dollar breaching 2.5200 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers agreed saying they thought market participants regarded 2.5200 ringgit as a sort of 'psychological level,' at which Bank Negara could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars as part of its policy of closely monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But most dealers doubted whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly at 2.5200 ringgit, but rather may just check to see how strong the demand for dollars was. \par \par \uc2  Dealers say they expect Thursday's trading range to again be narrow and within a range of between 2.5140 ringgit and around 2.5200 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  A Hong Kong-based dealer said he believed the low demand for the ringgit over the past few days was again partly influenced by the continued 'reverberations from the mid-May Thai baht crisis,' during which the ringgit also depreciated in a spillover effect. \par \par \uc2  'Funds are always faster to get out of a market than come back in,' the Hong Kong dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara didn't openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, at the late morning fixing, the one-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (Klibor) were at 8.19%, up from 8.02% Tuesday. The three-month Klibor were at 8.03%, up slightly from 7.96% Tuesday, while the six-month Klibor were at 7.94%, also up slightly from 7.89% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate, which indicates short-term liquidity conditions, closed at 8.5%, unchanged from Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0938GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt64041tu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
