\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Slightly Dn Early; Reflects Dlr Vs Majors \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 1997\par 05:26\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was down slightly against the U.S. dollar in early trading Tuesday, in subdued dealings which were again mainly influenced by the movement of the dollar against the majors. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there had been little buying interest in the ringgit so far Tuesday, but they noted the dollar's moves against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly in line with its moves against the majors. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign funds were still digesting the results of the weekend French election, which had encouraged them to buy dollars over increased uncertainty surrounding Europe's planned 1999 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union. \par \par \uc2  Dealers note that as the ringgit is closely linked to the majors, when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, or depreciates, against the majors, it usually follows the same trend against the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  At around 0316 GMT (1116 pm EDT), the dollar was at 2.5167 ringgit, up very slightly from 2.5162 ringgit late Monday, and 2.5155 ringgit early Monday. \par \par \uc2  A locally-based dealer said unless there was some major local news, he again expected later Tuesday trading to continue to be within a narrow range of between 2.5140 ringgit and 2.5195 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The local dealer, echoing the words of other dealers, said the dollar could touch the 2.5200 ringgit level, but he didn't think it would stay above this as players believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this level to sell dollars for ringgit. \par \par \uc2  'No-one knows for sure, but the 2.5200-ringgit-level is a sort of psychological barrier,' the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has traded between 2.5147 ringgit and 2.5175 ringgit so far this morning. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0326GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6304283\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
