\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit/Late -2: Strong Dollar Environment Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 1997\par 11:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A Hong Kong-based dealer said Tuesday trading, although more subdued than Monday's dealings, was still influenced by the 'strong dollar environment,' caused by the weekend French elections. \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dealer noted that the dollar had in general gained against the majors since the weekend, with many foreign funds buying dollars on increased jitters surrounding Europe's planned 1999 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  union. \par \par \uc2  Dealers noted that, as the ringgit is closely linked to the majors, when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, or depreciates, against the majors, it usually follows the same trend against the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  A locally-based dealer said this recent strong demand for the dollar had also kept many local players out of the market Tuesday, because they were 'confused about the market direction.' \par \par \uc2  Dealers said unless there is some domestic news to influence the market, they again expect Wednesday dealings to be dominated by the 'dollar play,' with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading in a narrow range of between 2.5150 ringgit and 2.5200 ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said they thought the dollar could break above 2.5200 ringgit, but they were unsure whether it would stay much above this level, owing to many player's belief that \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the market at this level, by selling dollars and buying ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara didn't openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In the money market, at the late morning fixing, the one-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (Klibor) were at 8.02%, up from 7.89% Monday. The three-month Klibor were at 7.96%, up from 7.85% Monday, while the six-month Klibor were at 7.89%, also up from 7.81% Monday. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate, which indicates short-term liquidity conditions, closed at 8.5%, unchanged from Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0912GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt63040ud\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
