\par\par \b \uc2  KL overnight steady after fall in interbank rates. \b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, May 27 (Reuter) - The overnight interbank rate was steady at 8.8/9.0 percent due to improved liquidity and a fall in interbank rates in the morning session, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The overnight indicated that interbank rates were returning to normalcy after two weeks of turbulence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The fall in rates started on Monday after heavy lending by big local banks in the one-month segment, said to be on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  No confirmation was available from Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it does not comment on its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped bring down the overnight rate to around nine percent on Monday from 18/20 before the weekend. \par \par \uc2  This brought down other interbank rates on Tuesday morning. \par \par \uc2  The dealers said movement of swaps to the left and continued lending by big banks aided in the easing of interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  One-week money was at 8.0/9.0 percent against 10/11 percent previously and two-week was at 8.0/9.0 percent against 9.0/11.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  One-month was at 7.5/8.0 percent against 8.5/9.0, while three-month and six-month were steady at 7.5/8.0 percent. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate on Monday fell to 8.0/8.5 percent from 18/20 percent on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "It helped that swaps have also been moving left (or easing) in the last few days," said a dealer with another Malaysian bank. \par \par \uc2  One-month swaps were quoting at 35/40 points on Tuesday, which translated into an implied yield of 7.3/4 percent, dealers said. A few days ago one-month had touched a high of 500, which implied a yield of 20 percent. \par \par \uc2  "The swaps are back to normal and so are the interbank rates," said a dealer with a European bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  He said the markets had calmed down after the interest rate rises caused by an aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the ringgit's fall two weeks ago. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was said to have sold around $1 billion. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drained liquidity from the system, causing the market to be short, and interbank rates to rise to unusually high levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Interest rate futures on the Malaysia Monetary Exchange were mixed as the selling triggered by interest rate falls were countered by covering of positions, futures dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the close, the three-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rate (KLIBOR) contract for June 1997 was unchanged at 92.49, or an implied yield of 7.51 percent. \par \par \uc2  September 1997 contract was down one point at 92.60, or 7.40 percent and December was down two at 92.60, or 7.40 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Madhav Reddy (603-230 7509) . \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5r04x5j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
