\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit/Late -2: Confusion Surrounds Klibor \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par 12:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Most dealers said the main reason for the strong appreciation in the\par ringgit Friday, had been the continued high Kuala Lumpur Interbank\par Offered Rates (Klibor).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Many overseas and local dealers believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised the\par three main Klibor on Thursday, to support its rumored \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par earlier in the week, by drawing players to the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and so\par keeping it from weakening further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  The ringgit had depreciated significantly Wednesday in what dealers said was a 'spillover effect' from the problems surrounding the Thai baht. \par \par \uc2  And many dealers widely believe \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday at around the 2.5248-ringgit-level, to stop the dollar appreciating above this level. \par \par \uc2  Friday's money market was filled with confusion surrounding the Klibor. At the late morning fixing, the one-month Kuala Lumpur Interbank Offered Rates (Klibor) were quoted as dropping slightly to 7.57%, down from 7.59% Thursday. The three-month Klibor were quoted at 7.53%, from 7.60% Thursday, while the six-month Klibor were at 7.53%, also down from 7.60% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But despite this apparent fall in the Klibor, many dealers said most banks were charging higher rates than those in the fixing. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a local bank said many banks had been too busy trading early Friday and hadn't had time to input their rates into the fixing average. He added that the one-month Klibor at his bank was 9.0%, the three-month Klibor was 8.5%, while the six-month Klibor were also at 8.5%. \par \par \uc2  Bank Negara didn't openly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money market Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1045GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5g03hoo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
