\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit/Early -2: Klibor Slightly Lower \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par 05:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong-based dealer said he thought the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action in raising the Klibor Thursday was a 'signal to speculators that they shouldn't attack the ringgit' like they have the Thai baht. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they widely believed \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday at the 2.5248-ringgit level, to stop the dollar strengthening above this level. \par \par \uc2  And a Singapore-based dealer said he thought the increase in the Klibor Thursday to levels not seen since February 1993 was to help further strengthen the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  In the money market Friday, at a later fixing than usual, all three Klibor were slightly lower. The one-month Klibor were at 7.57%, lower slighlty from 7.59% Thursday. The three-month Klibor were at 7.53%, also down from 7.60% Thursday, while the six-month Klibor also came down to 7.53%, from Thursday's 7.60%. \par \par \uc2  At around 0109 GMT (9:09 p.m. EDT) Friday, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached a high of 2.4730 ringgit. This means that from its level of 2.5245 ringgit late Wednesday to Friday's high, the ringgit has strengthened by 2.0% over the past two days. \par \par \uc2  A locally-based dealer said he didn't think the ringgit would strengthen much in later trading Friday, after the dramatic movements of the past few days. And he thought the dollar would trade between 2.4910 ringgit and 2.4950 ringgit for the rest of Friday dealings. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0356GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 