\par\par \b \uc2  Malaysia Ringgit Higher Early; Dlr-Majors Dominating \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par 05:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR (AP-Dow Jones)--The Malaysian ringgit was higher against the U.S. dollar in early trading Thursday, mainly on the back of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's falls against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Around 0350 GMT (11:50 p.m. EDT), the dollar was at 2.5177 ringgit, down from 2.5245 ringgit late Wednesday and 2.5225 ringgit early Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  A locally-based dealer said the dollar had weakened against the yen, largely because figures from the U.S. Wednesday showed that inflation wasn't rising. This made players feel interest rates won't be raised when the Federal Open Market Committee meets on May 20. If it appeared interest rates would rise, investors would tend to buy dollars to capitalize on the higher yield. \par \par \uc2  Dealers note that as the ringgit is closely linked to the majors, when the U.S. dollar appreciates or depreciates against the majors, it usually follows the same pattern against the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  A locally-based dealer said trading so far had been 'dollar/yen dominated,' noting that it had helped the ringgit recover from Wednesday's weakening. \par \par \uc2  Locally-based dealers, as well as those in Singapore and Hong Kong, widely believed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday at around the 2.5248-ringgit level, by selling dollars and buying the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to stop the dollar from strengthening above the 2.5250-ringgit level. \par \par \uc2  A dealer based in Hong Kong said the ringgit had weakened Wednesday, after a 'crisis situation' hit the Thai baht, on rumors of a possible devaluation. The weakening of the baht had a spillover effect as investors pulled out of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Most dealers said they didn't think the problems surrounding the Thai baht would have too much of an effect on the ringgit Thursday because the dollar is down so much against the yen and, therefore, trading in those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is dominating the Asian scene. \par \par \uc2  The locally-based dealer said he thought the dollar could weaken further to around the 2.5150-ringgit level in later Thursday trading. The dollar has traded between 2.5165 ringgit and 2.5215 ringgit so far this morning. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0359GMT \par \par \uc2  1026 1851 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5f03d20\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
