\par\par \b \uc2  Ringgit recovers but market remains jittery. \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KUALA LUMPUR, May 15 (Reuter) - The ringgit recovered in early Asian trading on profit-taking of dollar/ringgit positions after heavy selling of the Malaysian unit on Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The market looks a bit squarish at the moment, maybe people don't know what to do," said a European bank dealer in Kuala Lumpur. "Dollar/ringgit came down quite fast this morning but I expect some buying on dips." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said demand for the dollar from offshore centres would continue to weigh on the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  But worries about further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Bank Negara \b \highlight22\uc2 Malaysia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was limiting activity, they said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  strongly at 2.5250 late on Wednesday to stem the dollar's rise. A dealer with a European bank in Singapore said as high as $700 million could have been sold. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian unit came under heavy selling from foreign funds on Wednesday as weakness in the Thai baht, due to rising concerns about the slowing Thai economy and rumours of political turmoil within that country's cabinet, spilled over to regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the ringgit. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said softer dollar/majors also helped the ringgit's recovery. \par \par \uc2  At 0200 GMT, ringgit was at 2.5155/65 a dollar against 2.5240/50 at close of Kuala Lumpur on Wednesday. It had fallen to as low as 2.5260, its lowest level since January 3. \par \par \uc2  -- Syed Azman (603-206 2323) \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt5f05npu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\p